ntral entity in this community, serving as the location for the Unity March. This plaza is the common link between all other entities, suggesting its significance in the community. The plaza's association with the march could potentially lead to issues such as public disorder or conflict, depending on the nature of the march and the reactions it provokes. [Data: Entities (5), Relationships (37, 38, 39, 40, 41,+more)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Harmony Assembly's role in the community\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Harmony Assembly is another key entity in this community, being the organizer of the march at Verdant Oasis Plaza. The nature of Harmony Assembly and its march could be a potential source of threat, depending on their objectives and the reactions they provoke. The relationship between Harmony Assembly and the plaza is crucial in understanding the dynamics of this community. [Data: Entities(6), Relationships (38, 43)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Unity March as a significant event\",\n            \"explanation\": \"The Unity March is a significant event taking place at Verdant Oasis Plaza. This event is a key factor in the community's dynamics and could be a potential source of threat, depending on the nature of the march and the reactions it provokes. The relationship between the march and the plaza is crucial in understanding the dynamics of this community. [Data: Relationships (39)]\"\n        }},\n        {{\n            \"summary\": \"Role of Tribune Spotlight\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Tribune Spotlight is reporting on the Unity March taking place in Verdant Oasis Plaza. This suggests that the event has attracted media attention, which could amplify its impact on the community. The role of Tribune Spotlight could be significant in shaping public perception of the event and the entities involved. [Data: Relationships (40)]\"\n        }}\n    ]\n}}\n\n\n# Real Data\n\nUse the following text for your answer. Do not make anything up in your answer.\n\nText:\n-----Entities-----\nhuman_readable_id,title,description,degree\r\n7222,ADENOCARCINOMA DE PÁNCREAS,\"Adenocarcinoma de páncreas es un tipo de cáncer que se origina en el páncreas. En este caso, se ha diagnosticado en estadio IV, lo que indica que la enfermedad ha avanzado significativamente y presenta metástasis en el hígado y el bazo. Este tipo de tumor es conocido por su agresividad y se sospecha en pacientes que presentan diabetes de corta evolución o un empeoramiento de una diabetes preexistente.\",7\r\n2268,PÁNCREAS,\"The pancreas is a vital organ involved in digestion and metabolism, playing a crucial role in the secretion of digestive enzymes and fluids containing electrolytes into the small intestine. It can be adversely affected by various conditions, including cancer, which may lead to malabsorption issues and weight loss due to its impact on digestion. Additionally, the pancreas is susceptible to iron accumulation in conditions such as hemochromatosis. It is also a site where carcinoid tumors can develop, contributing to the secretion of serotonin, and where VIPomas and other neuroendocrine tumors may originate. Recently, a 3 cm nodule was identified in the pancreas during an urgent ultrasound examination, highlighting the importance of monitoring this organ for potential abnormalities.\",7\r\n607,EDEMA,\"Edema, also known as swelling, is a condition characterized by the accumulation of excess fluid in the body's tissues. It can manifest as a potential side effect of growth hormone treatment, indicating fluid retention within the body. Additionally, edema is a common complication associated with venous access, where fluid may accumulate due to various factors. In patients, edema may be observed as swelling resulting from this fluid retention. Furthermore, it can also be a sign of underlying health issues, such as malnutrition or other medical problems. Overall, edema represents a significant clinical concern that can arise from multiple causes, including medical treatments and health conditions.\",2\r\n606,EXPLORACIÓN FÍSICA,\"\"\"EXPLORACIÓN FÍSICA\"\" refers to a medical examination that plays a crucial role in identifying signs of malnutrition and diseases, particularly in patients with cirrhosis. This examination is a key method used in nutritional assessment to evaluate the overall health status of patients. It involves a thorough evaluation of the patient's physical condition, which is essential for determining nutritional status and general health, especially in critically ill patients, such as those undergoing hematopoietic cell transplantation. The process includes careful observation of physical signs related to the patient's nutritional state. Additionally, physical examination is a daily requirement for monitoring patients on parenteral nutrition, as it helps to check for potential issues such as dehydration or fluid overload. Overall, \"\"EXPLORACIÓN FÍSICA\"\" is an integral part of patient care, particularly for those with complex health needs.\",6\r\n625,DEPRESIÓN,\"Depresión, o depresión, es un trastorno del estado de ánimo que se caracteriza por una sensación persistente de tristeza y pérdida de interés, afectando la forma en que una persona se siente, piensa y maneja las actividades diarias. Esta condición es comúnmente observada como una comorbilidad psiquiátrica en pacientes con trastornos de la alimentación, donde a menudo se relaciona con alteraciones en los niveles de serotonina. Además, la depresión puede presentarse en pacientes con disfagia, debido al estrés y las complicaciones asociadas con esta condición.\n\nLa depresión también tiene un impacto significativo en la ingesta de alimentos y el estado nutricional, especialmente en pacientes con insuficiencia renal, donde puede influir negativamente en su alimentación. Asimismo, puede afectar el apetito y la ingesta de alimentos, contribuyendo a problemas nutricionales. En algunos casos, la depresión puede provocar alteraciones hormonales que son similares a las del síndrome de Cushing, aunque estas alteraciones son reversibles con el tratamiento adecuado. En resumen, la depresión no solo afecta el bienestar emocional, sino que también tiene implicaciones importantes en la salud física y nutricional de los individuos.\",7\r\n600,VALORACIÓN GLOBAL SUBJETIVA,\"The \"\"VALORACIÓN GLOBAL SUBJETIVA\"\" is a clinical tool designed for assessing nutritional status through a combination of clinical judgment, patient history, and physical examination. This method has been developed for various populations and serves as an effective means to evaluate a patient's nutritional condition. By integrating both subjective and objective data, the \"\"Valoración Global Subjetiva\"\" provides a comprehensive assessment of an individual's nutritional health.\",21\r\n8889,ANSIEDAD,\"Anxiety is another psychiatric condition frequently observed in patients with eating disorders, contributing to their overall psychological profile.\",2\r\n7252,PSICOFÁRMACOS,\"PSICOFÁRMACOS, or psychopharmaceuticals, are medications commonly employed in the treatment of various psychiatric conditions. They are particularly utilized to address depressive episodes in patients suffering from severe illnesses, such as cancer. Additionally, psychopharmaceuticals play a significant role in the management of eating disorders, helping to alleviate symptoms related to associated psychiatric conditions.\",2\r\n5747,SEROTONINA,\"Serotonina, or serotonin, is a neurotransmitter that plays a crucial role in various bodily functions. It is produced from the amino acid tryptophan and is primarily known for its involvement in regulating mood, intestinal permeability, weight control, and satiety. Additionally, serotonin has vasoconstrictive properties and is secreted by carcinoid tumors, which are a type of neuroendocrine tumor. In the liver, serotonin is metabolized to form 5-hydroxyindoleacetic acid (5-HIA). Furthermore, serotonin is mentioned in relation to the effects of tesofensina, a drug associated with weight loss. Overall, serotonin is a multifaceted substance that influences both psychological and physiological processes in the body.\",6\r\n7162,PARÁMETROS BIOQUÍMICOS,\"Los parámetros bioquímicos son análisis de sangre y otros fluidos corporales que desempeñan un papel fundamental en la evaluación del estado de salud y nutrición de los pacientes. Estos parámetros son especialmente cruciales en el seguimiento de aquellos que han sido sometidos a trasplante de células hematológicas. Además, se utilizan como indicadores en la valoración nutricional, permitiendo una evaluación más completa del estado de salud de un paciente.\",4\r\n5187,METÁSTASIS,\"METÁSTASIS refers to the process by which cancer cells spread from the original tumor site to other parts of the body. This phenomenon can involve various organs, including the liver, bones, and adrenal glands. Additionally, metastasis may be associated with the carcinoid syndrome, which is a group of symptoms that can occur in patients with certain types of cancer. Overall, METÁSTASIS signifies a critical aspect of cancer progression, highlighting the ability of cancer cells to invade and affect multiple areas beyond their initial location.\",2\r\n589,NÁUSEAS,\"NÁUSEAS refers to a symptom characterized by the sensation of needing to vomit, which can be associated with various medical conditions. This sensation of discomfort can interfere with food intake and negatively impact nutritional status. Nausea is particularly common among patients undergoing chemotherapy, often requiring dietary adjustments and the use of antiemetic medications to manage the condition effectively.\",2\r\n5753,TUMORES CARCINOIDES,\"TUMORES CARCINOIDES are tumors that can be diagnosed through the measurement of 5-Hydroxyindoleacetic acid (5-HIA). These tumors are derived from enterchromaffin cells, which are specialized cells found in the gastrointestinal tract that produce serotonin.\",7\r\n601,DETSKEY ET AL,Detsky et al. es un autor que ha contribuido a la metodología de la Valoración Global Subjetiva.,1\r\n616,DIFICULTAD PARA ALIMENTARSE,\"La dificultad para alimentarse se refiere a los problemas que un paciente puede experimentar al intentar comer, lo que puede afectar su estado nutricional.\",1\r\n617,FALTA DE APETITO,\"La falta de apetito es un síntoma que puede llevar a una disminución en la ingesta de alimentos y, por ende, a la desnutrición.\",1\r\n602,OTTERY,Ottery es un autor que modificó la Valoración Global Subjetiva en 1994.,1\r\n623,PROBLEMAS DENTALES,\"Los problemas dentales pueden interferir con la capacidad de un paciente para comer adecuadamente, afectando su nutrición.\",1\r\n626,PROBLEMAS ECONÓMICOS,\"Los problemas económicos pueden limitar el acceso a alimentos nutritivos, afectando el estado nutricional de un paciente.\",1\r\n609,PÉRDIDA DE TEJIDO ADIPOSO,La pérdida de tejido adiposo es un signo de desnutrición que se evalúa durante la valoración nutricional.,1\r\n5745,SÍNDROME CARCINOIDE,\"El síndrome carcinoide es una condición médica caracterizada por rubefacción, diarrea, y otros síntomas debido a la liberación de sustancias vasoactivas en la circulación sistémica.\",7\r\n5746,TRIPTÓFANO,\"Triptófano is an essential amino acid that plays a crucial role in various bodily functions, including the production of serotonin, a neurotransmitter that regulates mood, sleep, and appetite. In the body, triptófano is converted into serotonin, highlighting its importance in maintaining mental health and overall well-being. However, the metabolism of triptófano can be disrupted in patients with carcinoid syndrome, a condition that affects the body's ability to process this amino acid effectively. This alteration in metabolism can have significant implications for individuals suffering from this syndrome, emphasizing the need for understanding the role of triptófano in both health and disease.\",2\r\n13780,DATOS ANTROPOMÉTRICOS,\"Los datos antropométricos son medidas del cuerpo humano, como peso y altura, que se utilizan para evaluar el estado nutricional de los pacientes, especialmente en aquellos que han recibido un trasplante de células hematológicas.\",3\r\n14163,5-HIA,5-Hydroxyindoleacetic acid (5-HIA) is a metabolite of serotonin that is eliminated through urine and is used as a marker in diagnosing carcinoid tumors.,2\r\n14162,ACIDO 5-HIDROXIINDOLACETICO,A metabolite of serotonin that is eliminated in urine and is used to diagnose carcinoid tumors.,1\r\n5752,DÉFICIT DE NIACINA,\"El déficit de niacina es una condición que puede causar síntomas como lesiones cutáneas, relacionados con el síndrome carcinoide.\",1\r\n5749,ECOCARDIOGRAFÍA,\"ECOCARDIOGRAFÍA es un procedimiento diagnóstico médico que utiliza ultrasonido para evaluar tanto la estructura como la función del corazón. Este método es especialmente útil para detectar lesiones en pacientes que presentan síndrome carcinoide, lo que resalta su importancia en la identificación de condiciones cardíacas específicas.\",1\r\n5751,MASA TUMORAL,\"La masa tumoral se refiere al tamaño y extensión del tumor, que influye en la aparición del síndrome carcinoide.\",1\r\n14165,DIETA ESPECIAL,A special diet is required before urine collection for tests to avoid false positives in the determination of metabolites like 5-HIA and VAMA.,3\r\n\n\n-----Relationships-----\nhuman_readable_id,source,target,description,combined_degree\r\n3439,PACIENTE,ADENOCARCINOMA DE PÁNCREAS,\"El paciente fue diagnosticado con adenocarcinoma de páncreas, lo que define su condición médica\",553\r\n3107,PACIENTE,PÁNCREAS,\"Páncreas can experience malabsorption issues in pacientes with cancer, affecting their nutritional status\",553\r\n3377,PACIENTE,EDEMA,\"The patient experienced edema, which was monitored during their treatment\",548\r\n4375,EXPLORACIÓN FÍSICA,NUTRICIÓN PARENTERAL,Physical examination is a necessary par